<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.7.6: Lesson Synthesis</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01364</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.7.6: Lesson Synthesis</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f52d3747-03d7-4d20-8866-c747bd62e35f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Review how we can gather key information about situations from graphs representing them. Display one graph from the lesson, and ask:</para>
<list>
  <item>“How can you use the graph to determine the initial amount?”</item>
  <item>“How can you tell whether the growth factor is greater than 1 or less than 1?”</item>
  <item>“How can you use the graph to determine the growth factor?”</item>
  <item>“Once you know the initial amount and the growth factor, how can you construct an equation to represent the relationship?”</item>
</list></section>
</content>
</document>
